+::: {.callout-caution }
+## Jaccard index
+
+When calculating Jaccard index, it defaults to abundance weighted Jaccard
+dissimilarity which is similar to Bray-Curtis.
+
+```
+tse <- addDissimilarity(tse, assay.type = "counts", method = "jaccard")
+```
+
+To get the traditional Jaccard index (based on presence/absence), you can
+either transform data and calculate the index...
+
+```
+tse <- transformAssay(tse, method = "pa")
+tse <- addDissimilarity(tse, assay.type = "pa", method = "jaccard")
+```
+
+... or specify the `binary` flag.
+
+```
+tse <- addDissimilarity(
+    tse, assay.type = "counts", method = "jaccard",
+    binary = TRUE
+)
+```
+
+:::
+
